---
/**
 * Research — "The research" section.
 *
 * Recreates design/README.md §5 (The research) and the approved reference in
 * design/design-reference/Basset Landing.dc.html exactly: a left-aligned
 * section with the mono kicker "THE RESEARCH", the H2 grounding statement,
 * an intro paragraph, and a single bordered white 12px-radius list container
 * holding three rows (R1/R2/R3). Each row pairs a mono accent label with a
 * bold finding and a muted response. The section is separated from Mechanism
 * above it by a 1px hairline top border — the global rule the brief specifies
 * for section separation.
 *
 * Copy is verbatim per the brief. R2's finding contains straight double
 * quotes around "suspicious lines" as written in design/README.md §5.
 *
 * No screenshots or product imagery — this section is text-only per the
 * brief.
 *
 * Every color, size, spacing, radius, and copy string here is bound by the
 * brief; values live in src/styles/tokens.css and are read through the token
 * custom properties so a single change ripples across the site. QA verifies
 * against design/README.md §5 at 1440x900, 900x wide, 390x844, and 320x wide
 * (where the row's label column collapses above the finding).
 */
---

<section class="research" aria-labelledby="research-heading">
  <span class="kicker">The research</span>
  <h2 id="research-heading" class="research-heading">
    Built on how debugging actually works.
  </h2>

  <p class="intro">
    Before building Basset we studied the research on how developers actually find root causes. Three findings shaped the product:
  </p>

  <div class="list">
    <div class="row">
      <span class="label">R1</span>
      <div class="content">
        <p class="finding">
          Developers spend roughly half of debugging time hunting for the right code, not fixing it.
        </p>
        <p class="response">
          So Basset attacks the hunt: from a log line straight to the statement that wrote it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <span class="label">R2</span>
      <div class="content">
        <p class="finding">
          Ranked lists of "suspicious lines" fail in practice; developers need the causal story, not a leaderboard.
        </p>
        <p class="response">
          So Basset shows a walkable chain of what happened, with evidence at each step.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="row">
      <span class="label">R3</span>
      <div class="content">
        <p class="finding">
          Engineers distrust tools that hide their reasoning.
        </p>
        <p class="response">
          So every Basset answer traces back to real code and the real run, and the tool says honestly where its visibility ends.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /* Section container — the brief's global separation rule: a 1px hairline
     top border between sections, with fluid vertical padding. Left-aligned
     block, matching the hero and every other section. */
  .research {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    padding: var(--section-padding-y) 0;
    text-align: left;
  }

  /* Kicker — mono, uppercase, spaced accent. text-transform lets the source
     stay in sentence case (matching the design reference's markup) while
     rendering in caps. */
  .kicker {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--font-size-kicker);
    letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-kicker);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }

  /* Section H2 — the global h2 rule in BaseLayout already applies the type
     tokens (family/size/weight/line-height/letter-spacing); we add the
     vertical rhythm below the kicker and pin ink color defensively so a
     global tweak cannot mute it. */
  .research-heading {
    margin: 16px 0 0;
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* Intro paragraph — 16px/26px muted per the brief. 66ch measure keeps the
     line count balanced under the H2. */
  .intro {
    margin: clamp(20px, 3vw, 32px) 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--color-muted);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  /* List container — a single bordered white card with a 12px radius that
     holds the three rows. overflow: hidden clips the inter-row hairlines to
     the radius so the dividers align cleanly with the container's rounded
     edges. */
  .list {
    margin-top: clamp(24px, 3vw, 40px);
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
    border-radius: var(--radius-card);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  /* Row — a two-column grid with a fixed 56px label column and a fluid
     content column. align-items: baseline drops the mono label onto the
     first line of the finding at the wider breakpoint. The gap between
     grid columns is 16px per the brief; row padding is 22px 24px. */
  .row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr;
    gap: 16px;
    align-items: baseline;
    padding: 22px 24px;
  }

  /* Row divider — a 1px hairline between rows, applied to every row after
     the first via the adjacent-sibling combinator. That leaves the first
     row without a top border and the last row without a bottom border, so
     both flush against the list container's rounded edges. */
  .row + .row {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-hairline);
  }

  /* Row label — mono 12.5px 600 accent. The size matches the section
     kicker's 12.5px per the brief's row spec. */
  .label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12.5px;
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-accent-text);
  }

  /* Row content stack — holds the finding and its response. margin: 0 on
     both paragraphs resets the browser default so the 6px gap between them
     is the sole source of separation. */
  .content {
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* Finding — 16px/26px 600 ink. The bold weight and ink color contrast
     the muted response below it. */
  .finding {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    font-weight: var(--weight-semibold);
    color: var(--color-ink);
  }

  /* Response — 16px/26px muted, 6px below the finding. */
  .response {
    margin: 6px 0 0;
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--font-size-body);
    line-height: var(--line-height-body);
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  /* Narrow-width responsive collapse — below ~420px the 56px label column
     becomes cramped, so drop the row to a single column with the label
     sitting on its own line above the finding. The label keeps a 4px gap
     from the finding via its own bottom margin, and row padding tightens
     slightly for the narrower viewport. */
  @media (max-width: 420px) {
    .row {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      padding: 20px 20px;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .label {
      margin-bottom: 4px;
    }
  }
</style>
